              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to howl, then the Marathi for to crackle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: दुष्काळ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दुष्काळ — duṣkāḷ — \"a drought; a famine\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "त्या वर्षी मोठा दुष्काळ पडला. tyā varṣī moṭhā duṣkāḷ paḍlā. That year there was a great drought."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दुष्काळ (duṣkāḷ) पडणे, a drought strikes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दुष्काळ (duṣkāḷ) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit duṣkāla, \"a bad time, a famine\" (CDIAL 6470), where CDIAL also lists the inherited Marathi dukāḷ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
